OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1776025044
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G13/13
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, SWAPO guerrillas are returning directly
OL,6, to Angola from Namibia and avoiding UN
OL,7, assembly points, says their leader.
OL,9,FMr Sam Nujoma described the assembly
OL,10,Fpoints as a South African trap to
OL,11,Fcapture the guerrillas.
OL,13,FThe points were set up to monitor the
OL,14,FSWAPO rebels' departure from Namibia,
OL,15,Ffollowing their incursion on April 1.
OL,17,FAt least 290 SWAPO guerrillas and South
OL,18,FAfrican-led forces have been killed in
OL,19,Ffighting since the incursion, which
OL,20,Fhas held up moves towards Namibian
OL,21,Findependence.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
